{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>If as a thanksgiving offering he offers it.</b> The thanksgiving offering requires laying on of hands, and waving after slaughter." "<b>And he shall bring upon the slaughter-offering.</b> With the slaughter-offering; and likewise על חלת לחם — a model: it is reckoned על שדה הארץ (like a field of the land)." "<b>And fine flour soaked.</b> We learn for the soaked offering that it must be fine flour." "<b>Cake kneaded with oil.</b> This is an inclusion after an inclusion, to exclude: it is not like other meal-offerings, which have a log of oil, but rather half of it."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "The phrase על שדה הארץ may be a shorthand allusion to the valuation formula in Lev 27:16; the connection is terse and not fully spelled out."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:10:28.004156348Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}